01:01:30.774 --> 01:01:32.040
that that was--

01:01:32.040 --> 01:01:34.260
He was under the influence of--

01:01:34.260 --> 01:01:36.520
Not at that time.
Of joy, man.

01:01:36.520 --> 01:01:39.580
He was under the impression that

01:01:39.580 --> 01:01:42.083
this is the correct response to what's up.

01:01:43.300 --> 01:01:44.920
And I don't know if we
ever talked about it.

01:01:44.920 --> 01:01:49.450
I don't know 100% that he
didn't do it for effect

01:01:49.450 --> 01:01:51.940
but we never discussed it.

01:01:51.940 --> 01:01:53.820
There were a lot of things about Gregg

01:01:53.820 --> 01:01:58.049
that we didn't wanna
pull back the curtain.

01:01:58.049 --> 01:01:59.380
Just let him be Gregg.

01:01:59.380 --> 01:02:04.380
Yeah it's like it's better to
just take it at face value.

01:02:04.400 --> 01:02:05.550
Yeah.
Just like

01:02:05.550 --> 01:02:08.017
whenever we'd talk about
studying and he'd say,

01:02:08.017 --> 01:02:11.227
"Man, you know what you know.

01:02:11.227 --> 01:02:12.620
"You don't learn anything."

01:02:12.620 --> 01:02:14.280
Yeah.

01:02:14.280 --> 01:02:18.908
That sounds like a sound
reasoning, foundation,

01:02:18.908 --> 01:02:20.660
to not do my homework.

01:02:20.660 --> 01:02:21.777
And I think, I've gotten--

01:02:21.777 --> 01:02:24.180
And you fell for that a lot.
I've gotten many tweets

01:02:24.180 --> 01:02:27.020
from people who say that

01:02:27.020 --> 01:02:29.446
they are employing Gregg's philosophy.

01:02:29.446 --> 01:02:30.600
You know what you know.

01:02:30.600 --> 01:02:31.510
I sat down to study

01:02:31.510 --> 01:02:33.790
and then I just remember what Gregg said.

01:02:33.790 --> 01:02:36.260
I don't think that's great
advice if your goal is

01:02:36.260 --> 01:02:38.060
to make good grades.

01:02:38.060 --> 01:02:40.590
If your goal is just to
enjoy yourself while you're

01:02:40.590 --> 01:02:43.820
in school and not really use the degree

01:02:43.820 --> 01:02:47.363
that you're getting,
then that's good advice.

01:02:48.510 --> 01:02:50.750
I'm not using my engineering
degree so it worked for me.

01:02:50.750 --> 01:02:54.120
We did a RhettandLinKast
and we had Gregg call in

01:02:54.120 --> 01:02:56.390
and we had a discussion with Gregg.

01:02:56.390 --> 01:02:57.600
I don't know if that one's been posted

01:02:57.600 --> 01:02:59.330
to the Mythical Society.

01:02:59.330 --> 01:03:02.570
I don't believe it has but I
do remember that happening.

01:03:02.570 --> 01:03:03.403
Hmm.

01:03:04.538 --> 01:03:06.700
Okay that's all the questions, we--

01:03:06.700 --> 01:03:08.380
Gregg with three Gs, love you man.

01:03:08.380 --> 01:03:10.640
We took some time on those questions.

01:03:10.640 --> 01:03:12.200
We'll get to more
questions next time we do

01:03:12.200 --> 01:03:13.578
an episode like this.

01:03:13.578 --> 01:03:16.037
♪ Rec baby rec baby one two three four ♪

01:03:16.037 --> 01:03:19.640
♪ Rec baby rec baby one two ♪

01:03:19.640 --> 01:03:21.970
Rec baby rec baby one.

01:03:21.970 --> 01:03:24.790
I forgot I had to give a rec so I'm like--

01:03:24.790 --> 01:03:26.743
Scrambling.
Racking my brain.

01:03:29.115 --> 01:03:32.880
I was coming home, I was
gonna leave for work yesterday

01:03:32.880 --> 01:03:35.696
and Christy sent me a text, she was like,

01:03:35.696 --> 01:03:39.123
we got a teenager party
happening over here.

01:03:40.750 --> 01:03:43.240
Lily had a bunch of her friends over.

01:03:43.240 --> 01:03:45.300
And we're trying to be that house

01:03:45.300 --> 01:03:47.040
where the friends come over and hang out

01:03:47.040 --> 01:03:48.090
'cause we think that,

01:03:49.890 --> 01:03:52.480
that way we can be in the mix, you know.

01:03:52.480 --> 01:03:56.087
We can have our pulse on what's happening

01:03:56.087 --> 01:03:57.690
and the friend group.

01:03:57.690 --> 01:04:00.080
You can have your finger on the pulse.

01:04:00.080 --> 01:04:01.610
I don't think you get to have the pulse.

01:04:01.610 --> 01:04:02.660
Right, right.

01:04:02.660 --> 01:04:05.640
Yeah we're not, Christy
tells me to keep my distance,

01:04:05.640 --> 01:04:09.280
not to try to bop, get
in there and be cool Dad.

01:04:09.280 --> 01:04:10.820
Just stay on the fringe.
Right.

01:04:10.820 --> 01:04:13.040
Or be the guy who picks
up stuff that they need

01:04:13.040 --> 01:04:17.273
and they wanted to roast
marshmallows on our fire pit.

01:04:19.770 --> 01:04:22.670
I was like you know what, we've
been needing to get these.

01:04:23.890 --> 01:04:27.220
And so I went to the
REI and I'm recommending

01:04:27.220 --> 01:04:30.040
that you go to the REI and get,

01:04:30.040 --> 01:04:35.040
they got these fancy skewers.

01:04:35.350 --> 01:04:36.595
Oh wow.
I love it when someone

01:04:36.595 --> 01:04:39.419
has thought about everything
associated with something

01:04:39.419 --> 01:04:44.419
that you can just get a dumb metal version

01:04:44.940 --> 01:04:46.090
to poke your eye out with.

01:04:46.090 --> 01:04:48.350
It's fully retractable.

01:04:48.350 --> 01:04:51.160
It's like a pointer,
it retracts in and out.

01:04:51.160 --> 01:04:52.352
How much is this?

01:04:52.352 --> 01:04:54.870
$13.
Apiece?

01:04:54.870 --> 01:04:55.810
You get two of 'em.

01:04:55.810 --> 01:04:57.130
Well how many did you buy for this group

01:04:57.130 --> 01:04:59.520
of 20 kids that were at your house?

01:04:59.520 --> 01:05:00.890
Well you know me, well--

01:05:00.890 --> 01:05:02.581
You probably got four of 'em.

01:05:02.581 --> 01:05:05.692
I got two packs which is four total.

01:05:05.692 --> 01:05:07.330
And I told Lily, I was like--
So they're doing four

01:05:07.330 --> 01:05:09.560
at a time and just sitting
around watching each other?

01:05:09.560 --> 01:05:10.780
Well it's a party, man.

01:05:10.780 --> 01:05:12.393
That's part of it, you watch.

01:05:12.393 --> 01:05:13.833
You should have gotten
enough skewers for people

01:05:13.833 --> 01:05:17.330
to pack into your fire pit
which I think 12 people

01:05:17.330 --> 01:05:18.240
could be in the fire pit.

01:05:18.240 --> 01:05:20.184
I told Lily--
It should have been 12.

01:05:20.184 --> 01:05:21.790
I was like I think, when I
brought 'em home I was like,

01:05:21.790 --> 01:05:23.800
I think you should, I
was like bragging about

01:05:23.800 --> 01:05:25.400
look what I got, they're retractable,

01:05:25.400 --> 01:05:27.300
they got the fork on the end and look,

01:05:27.300 --> 01:05:29.850
you can hold the handle
and rotate your thumb

01:05:29.850 --> 01:05:32.171
and it will twist the entire thing

01:05:32.171 --> 01:05:36.040
for perfect marshmallow
roasting but with these four

01:05:36.040 --> 01:05:38.100
that I've got, I would
recommend that you choose--

01:05:38.100 --> 01:05:39.820
You didn't even get enough
for your own family.

01:05:39.820 --> 01:05:41.010
Designated roast.

01:05:41.010 --> 01:05:42.650
You didn't even get enough for the Neals.

01:05:42.650 --> 01:05:44.037
They're expensive, man.
There's five of you.

01:05:44.037 --> 01:05:45.360
$12.

01:05:45.360 --> 01:05:47.653
This is a, what are you gonna do

01:05:47.653 --> 01:05:49.480
when your family's roasting marshmallows?

01:05:49.480 --> 01:05:51.461
There's gonna be one odd person out.

01:05:51.461 --> 01:05:53.490
Everybody doesn't need to roast.

01:05:53.490 --> 01:05:55.823
Someone's on graham cracker duty.

01:05:56.670 --> 01:05:58.100
Somebody's on chocolate duty.

01:05:58.100 --> 01:06:01.140
Somebody's an assembler and
some people are roasters.

01:06:01.140 --> 01:06:02.600
I make everybody do all their s'mores.

01:06:02.600 --> 01:06:04.550
Some people are better
roasters than others

01:06:04.550 --> 01:06:06.570
and if you give everybody roasters,

01:06:06.570 --> 01:06:08.203
eyes are gonna be poked out.

01:06:09.250 --> 01:06:10.260
It's all part of it.

01:06:10.260 --> 01:06:11.520
Marshmallows are gonna be burnt.

01:06:11.520 --> 01:06:13.690
One person going to the
emergency room is part

01:06:13.690 --> 01:06:15.163
of your first camping trip.

01:06:17.520 --> 01:06:18.900
It's a rite of passage.

01:06:18.900 --> 01:06:21.903
I found an awesome thing
and I ain't buying too many.

01:06:23.310 --> 01:06:26.190
So you're recommending this but--

01:06:26.190 --> 01:06:27.237
Yeah, four man.

01:06:28.630 --> 01:06:30.010
I'll add a rec to the rec,

01:06:30.010 --> 01:06:32.631
I think you should get
one per family member.

01:06:32.631 --> 01:06:35.050
Then if I had to, there are two in a pack,

01:06:35.050 --> 01:06:36.720
so I would have had one extra.

01:06:36.720 --> 01:06:38.520
That's wasteful.
Give it to Jade.

01:06:39.410 --> 01:06:41.630
Or it's back-up for when one breaks.

01:06:41.630 --> 01:06:44.060
They sound like they've
got a lot of moving parts.

01:06:44.060 --> 01:06:45.643
I'm the designated roaster.

01:06:47.040 --> 01:06:48.950
Well then you only need one.

01:06:48.950 --> 01:06:51.213
Two hands, two back-ups.

01:06:53.890 --> 01:06:55.940
So is this an official REI brand thing

01:06:55.940 --> 01:06:57.440
or you just can get it at REI?

01:06:58.810 --> 01:07:00.350
You just get it at REI.

01:07:00.350 --> 01:07:01.730
You can't get it at the grocery store

01:07:01.730 --> 01:07:03.580
which is where I was gonna
go until Jenna told me

01:07:03.580 --> 01:07:04.710
to go to Ralphs.

01:07:04.710 --> 01:07:06.300
This is Jenna's rec.

01:07:06.300 --> 01:07:07.910
Ralphs?

01:07:07.910 --> 01:07:09.200
REI.
REI.

01:07:09.200 --> 01:07:11.280
I was gonna go to Ralphs.

01:07:11.280 --> 01:07:12.680
But you got--
But she recommended REI.

01:07:12.680 --> 01:07:14.730
Did you get the marshmallows at Ralphs

01:07:14.730 --> 01:07:16.610
or did you get marshmallows
at REI as well?

01:07:16.610 --> 01:07:17.860
I didn't get marshmallows.

01:07:17.860 --> 01:07:18.910
They already had 'em.

01:07:19.828 --> 01:07:20.661
Oh.

01:07:22.740 --> 01:07:24.440
You're welcome.
There you go.

